# AR Calendar — Microsoft 365 authoritative source

**Full doc:** `docs/AR-CALENDAR-MICROSOFT-365-NATIVE-ACTIONS.md`

## Product

- Transovo Calendar is **read-only** — no create, edit, delete, or drag-and-drop in Transovo.
- **Create / update** — customer uses Outlook on the web (or Google when connected).
- **SMS reschedule** — existing Appointment Reminders Graph workflow (do not replace).
- **Calendar mirror** — import/display **all** events from selected calendars (`isEventEligibleForCalendarMirror`).
- **SMS reminders** — `isEventEligibleForReminderImport` + `reminderSmsEligible` metadata only; never hide mirror events for reminder rules.

## Native Microsoft 365 actions (Calendar header)

| Button | Behavior |
|--------|----------|
| Add appointment | `https://outlook.office.com/calendar/deeplink/compose` (new tab) |
| Open Outlook | `https://outlook.office.com/calendar/` |
| Add calendar | Outlook calendar UI — `manageCalendarsUrl` from native-actions API |

Deep links are convenience URLs, not a stable Graph contract. API: `GET /api/appointment-reminders/calendar/native-actions`.

## Automatic sync (reuse — do not duplicate)

- Graph change notifications (`created`, `updated`, `deleted`) — `src/lib/calendar/webhooks.ts`
- Webhook ingress — `/api/integrations/calendars/webhooks/microsoft`
- Delta / missed notifications — `microsoft-delta-sync.ts`, `import-sync.ts`
- AR stale backstop — `maybe-sync-stale-calendars.ts`
- UI: refetch on window focus + **Sync now**; background sync runs without the page open

Subscriptions target the connected user’s mailbox events — not every shared calendar without extra permissions. New Outlook calendars must be **selected** under Calendar connections.

## Before changing scopes or subscription shape

Audit OAuth scopes, connected calendar IDs, reminder job suppression, and existing SMS reschedule Graph code.
